Vanta: restore Firefox's cookie banner handling (toolkit/components/cookiebanners).

Mozilla removed this feature in Firefox 155 (bug 2058143, parts 7 and 8, hg
revs c3b49c86ffa0 and dfc9e3c70dca). This patch is those removals reversed,
against Firefox 157.0.1, limited to what desktop needs:

  - toolkit/components/cookiebanners/ (service, cookie injector, actors, tests)
  - the cookiebanners.* static and runtime prefs
  - the CookieBanner JSWindowActor registration
  - nsILoadInfo.hasInjectedCookieForCookieBannerHandling and its IPC field
  - the Glean metrics registration and the rules-list Remote Settings dump
  - the clear-data integration, so "Forget About This Site" and
    Clear-Site-Data also reset per-site cookie banner state (flag bits 26
    and 27, which Mozilla left vacant)

Left out on purpose: the protections-panel/settings UI, Nimbus feature, legacy
Telemetry scalars (the Glean metrics' telemetry_mirror lines are dropped), the
Android/GeckoView API, and lint/docs/perf-test references.

Every line here is Mozilla's own code. Vanta's changes are in cookiebanners-2.

